From 7f5e9fc66d7c0e3015bf2ceccf66af5909e8824c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LiinkPK <linkgarciafiverr@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 02:33:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HUD scaling fixes for Story Mode, notices, gauges and the
 Chess and Open World screens; HD subtitles with a baked outline; the HUD
 settings section is named HUD

- New marker modes for the profile's layouts: corner (Chess and Open World corner HUD), box (map description window), banner,
  notice (ASSIST bar) and keep (EX Finisher gauges and inputs left as drawn).
- The skill-name message box scales as one piece wherever it sits; the assist gauge's masks and sweep strips take their side.
- Subtitles are told by how they are drawn (centred near the bottom, 18 pixels tall; in battle, inside the mode 0x14 layout),
  not by their heap. Their line image is built at 6 texels per pixel with a smooth outline baked into the letters; the game's
  four dark outline copies are drawn empty. All five copies shrink about one point (Subtitle size and height), and Text > Size
  no longer changes subtitles.
- NVIDIA GPUs with device id 0x2900 or above upload textures synchronously (menu text was drawn as flat blocks);
  <prefix>_ASYNC_UPLOADS=1 keeps the background uploads.
- The debug triggers and traces (F10 text trace, HUD quad dump, roster trace) are written to logs/; the text trace lists each
  text-line quad's final place ([text-quad]).
- A debug dump of what the HUD rule does to each piece (hud_quads.txt) with <prefix>_TRACE_HUD_LAYOUTS set and F10.
